RUBIK'S CUBE IDENTITIES

I'm trying to find a presentation for the Rubik's cube group, generated by
quarter-turn face moves, with relations of minimal length.

The original reason for this was to create an Anki deck for memorizing OLL/PLL
algorithms. I wanted each flash card to present and have me do the inverse
algorithm, then have me do the forward algorithm from memory. But doing the
inverse algorithm myself gives me too much information to accurately test my
memory, so I wanted to embed some JavaScript to "jumble" the inverse algorithm a
bit by applying some transformations. Group theoretically, I wanted some
relations in the group presentation.

The main program is `find_rels.c`.

	It's a multithreaded program to search for move sequences that leave the
	cube unchanged, i.e. relations.

	It will produce several files (at least 1 per thread) containing these
	relations.

	It can be stopped mid-calculation and resume almost right where
	it left off.

	To compile, just run `make`.

The directory `rel12` is the computed result of `find_rels.c` as currently
configured.

	I included it because it's not much (just 32 relations) and takes quite some
	time to compute.

The script `all_reorients.py` operates on the output of `find_rels.c`.

	For efficiency, `find_rels.c` will only search for relations that are of a
	specific orientation.

	This script produces, for each relation outputted, all 48-or-less relations
	that are essentially the same, up to some cube rotation / mirror.

The script `pretty_print.py` just prints the algorithms in standard Rubik's cube
notation.

Upon cloning this repo, you can run
	$ cat rel12/* | python all_reorients.py | python pretty_print.py
to see all 1,536 12-move algorithms which leave the cube unchanged.

	There are more than this, but they are redundant, including parts like:
		U U'
		U3
		D U (where another otherwise identical algorithm has U D)
